    "body": "This makes it more friendly to Ractor workers which, provided they never need a reload, won't have to write to the Reloader module instance variable.\r\n\r\nI found this while making Active Job ractor-safe. Since the `active_job.set_reloader_hook` initializer calls `wrap` on the reloader, and the reloader's `run!` method is overridden to call `check!`, `check!` can't write if it's called from a Ractor (I don't have a ractor job adapter, but I was testing with the inline adapter from a request).\r\n\r\nEven if the check says to never reload (Edit: ~in `ractorize!`~ the default), we always wrote to the instance variable because of the `||=`.",
    "created_at": "2026-09-09T16:30:26Z",
    "updated_at": "2026-09-10T21:18:20Z",
    "closed_at": "2026-09-10T21:18:18Z",
